# UniShare.lk — Student Resource Hub

ICT 1209 – Web Technologies | Mini Project (Phase 3: PHP & MySQL Integration)

A student resource-sharing platform where users register, log in, and
upload/browse study materials (notes, slides, lab reports, videos, past
papers) organised by category.

## Tech Stack
- HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap-style custom CSS
- Vanilla JavaScript (client-side validation, UI interactions)
- PHP 8 (server-side logic, PDO + MySQLi-style prepared statements)
- MySQL (via XAMPP/WAMP)

## Folder Structure
```
project/
├── css/            Stylesheets (one per page, + shared.css for auth/dashboard/resources)
├── js/              Vanilla JS (form validation, UI effects)
├── images/          Logo and hero images
├── includes/
│   ├── db.php              PDO database connection
│   ├── functions.php       Session, auth-guard, and helper functions
│   ├── header.php          Shared, auth-aware navbar
│   └── footer.php          Shared footer
├── auth/
│   ├── register.php        Sign up (bcrypt password hashing)
│   ├── login.php            Log in (session_regenerate_id on success)
│   └── logout.php           Clean session teardown
├── uploads/          Uploaded resource files (protected via .htaccess)
├── contact.php        Contact form → saved to `messages` table
├── index.php           Home page
├── features.php        Features page
├── about.php            About page
├── resources.php        Public resource browser (search + category filter)
├── dashboard.php        Protected: upload resources, view your own uploads
├── database.sql         Full schema (users, messages, resources)
└── README.md
```

## Setup Instructions (XAMPP)

1. **Install & start XAMPP.** Start the **Apache** and **MySQL** modules from
   the XAMPP control panel.

2. **Copy the project folder** into your XAMPP web root, e.g.:
   ```
   C:\xampp\htdocs\unishare\
   ```
   (On macOS: `/Applications/XAMPP/htdocs/unishare/`)

3. **Import the database.**
   - Open `http://localhost/phpmyadmin`
   - Click **Import**, choose `database.sql`, and click **Go**.
   - This creates the `unishare` database with `users`, `messages`, and
     `resources` tables.
   - Alternatively, from a terminal: `mysql -u root -p < database.sql`
   - Then also import **`database_additions.sql`** the same way (or
     `mysql -u root -p unishare < database_additions.sql`). This adds the
     `comments`, `bookmarks`, and `todos` tables used by the Features page
     (Comments, Bookmarks & Save, and To Do List).

4. **Check the DB credentials** in `includes/db.php` match your XAMPP setup.
   The defaults (`root` user, empty password, `localhost`) work for a
   standard XAMPP install with no changes needed.

5. **Open the site** in your browser:
   ```
   http://localhost/unishare/index.php
   ```

6. **Create an account** via the "Sign up" button, then log in. From the
   dashboard you can upload a resource; it will then appear on the public
   Resources page for everyone to browse and download.

## Security Notes
- Passwords are hashed with `password_hash()` (`PASSWORD_BCRYPT`) — never
  stored in plain text.
- All database queries use **prepared statements** (PDO) to prevent SQL
  injection.
- `session_regenerate_id()` is called on successful login to prevent
  session fixation.
- All user-supplied output is escaped with `htmlspecialchars()` before being
  printed, to prevent XSS.
- The `uploads/` folder has a `.htaccess` rule blocking execution of any
  uploaded PHP file.
- Every form is validated **both** client-side (JavaScript, for instant
  feedback) and server-side (PHP, because JavaScript can be bypassed).

## Notes
- The Post/Redirect/Get pattern is used on `contact.php`, `dashboard.php`,
  and the auth pages, so refreshing the page after a submission never
  resubmits the form.
- `includes/header.php` reads the session to show either "Log in / Sign up"
  or "Dashboard / Log out" in the navbar automatically.
